  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "For every dollar Ben spent on bagels, David spent \\(25\\) cents less. Ben paid \\(\\$12.50\\) more than David. How much did they spend in the bagel store together?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$37.50\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$50.00\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$87.50\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$90.00\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$92.50\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "For every \\(\\$1\\) Ben spends, David spends \\(\\$0.25\\) less. Thus their difference is \\(25\\%\\), or \\(0.25\\), of Ben's spending. Dividing the known difference by this fraction recovers Ben's full spending:\n\\[\n12.50\\div0.25=50.\n\\]\nBen spends \\(\\$50\\), so David spends \\(\\$50-\\$12.50=\\$37.50\\). Together they spend\n\\[\n\\$50+\\$37.50=\\boxed{\\$87.50},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
